{
  "abstract": "We conduct a controlled 3-seed (`Seeds 42, 101, 7`) diagnostic audit of a critic-free 4-stage `GRPO` adaptation of Fast-and-Slow RLVR (`Thinker`, arXiv:2505.21097: Fast $L_{\\text{fast}}=512$, Verification $L_{\\text{verify}}=256$, Slow $L_{\\text{slow}}=1024$, Summarization $L_{\\text{sum}}=512$) on `Qwen3-0.6B-Base` across 22 `Pool950` runs (`Val210` + `Ext240` + training-disjoint `MATH-500`; `62,700` mode predictions, `0/950` training overlap) and a 50-step factorial token-ID probe (`thinker_bcd_no_a2_s42`). First, while 50-step `Thinker-Baseline` (`141.0k` tokens, `31.3` active updates) beats 50-step single-turn `Fast-Only QA GRPO` ($L=512$, `57.1k` tokens, `18.7` updates) on `Fast@512` ($435.67 \\pm 15.28$ vs. $403.67 \\pm 29.37$) and `Fast@2048` ($479.67 \\pm 12.22$ vs. $456.67 \\pm 47.50$), an approximately update- and token-matched 90-step $L=1024$ `Fast-Only QA GRPO` control (`144.4k` tokens, `33.0` updates) reaches $434.00 \\pm 8.19$ on `Fast@512` and $492.67 \\pm 3.21$ on `Fast@2048`, demonstrating no advantage of 50-step 4-stage `Thinker` over this approximately matched single-turn control. Second, newest-entry FIFO self-replay SFT (`Thinker-Naive-SFT`, dominated by `141/143` Fast-response replay steps) degrades `Fast@512` on 3/3 seeds ($418.00 \\pm 7.21$, $-17.67$ items). Third, on `Pool950` `Thinker-Full`, `Thinker-Baseline` ($437.00 \\pm 14.73$), `Thinker-BCD` ($438.00 \\pm 4.36$), `Thinker-BCD-Concise` ($437.67 \\pm 19.04$), and 90-step $L=1024$ `GRPO` ($437.33 \\pm 5.51$) show no aggregate capability advance, though the coupled `BCD` packages increase `MATH-500` negative verification recall ($12.19\\%$ to $16.09\\%\\text{--}23.12\\%$) and net Slow rescues ($+1.33 \\pm 0.58$ to $+11.00 \\pm 4.58$ and $+8.67 \\pm 8.74$ items). Fourth, direct token-ID comparison confirms that in-dialogue Stage 4 copies all $512$ leading Stage-3 tokens (`LCP=512`) on $6/8$ ($75.0\\%$) of $>512$-token rescues ($16/19 = 84.2\\%$ in runtime logs).",
